{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAoZWUufdUt3J6AvueRD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the findings to `ANSWER.md`. I did not change `server.py`, and nothing was sent anywhere outside this machine.\n\nI ran the server locally on port 62767 and sent it requests with curl. The most serious problem is that malformed input crashes the request handler, so the client gets an empty reply instead of a JSON-RPC error. I confirmed four cases in the server log: a bare JSON string body, `arguments` given as a string, an array `id` to `get_note`, and `add_note` without `title`.\n\nThe other problems that matter most for real clients:\n\n- **Anonymous `resources/list` returns HTTP 401.** The server advertises the resources capability, so clients that list resources on connect may fail.\n- **Anonymous `add_note` returns a 401 with a body that isn't JSON-RPC** and no `WWW-Authenticate` header. The client can't match the reply to its request.\n- **Notifications other than `notifications/initialized` get replies**, which the spec forbids.\n- **Chunked request bodies are silently misread** as `method not found: None`.\n- **The protocol version is not negotiated.** The server always answers `2025-06-18`.\n\n`ANSWER.md` also has lower-severity spec deviations, things that work, and a suggested fix order. Two non-client issues are worth knowing: `add_note` writes are lost on restart, and the default token `dev-token-123` is in both the code and the README.\n\nI did not test against a real client, so whether the 401 and version problems break Claude Code, Codex or Gemini is unconfirmed. I stopped the test server afterwards and removed my scratch log, so the only change in the directory is `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2331,"cache_read_input_tokens":39572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_in